## Code Review: Transaction Consistency Bug

### 🔴 Critical Issue Identified

**File:** `src/main/java/com/example/invoice/InvoiceService.java`  
**Line:** 20-22

```java
domainEventPublisher.publish("invoice.approved", invoiceId);  // ❌ Published BEFORE commit
invoiceRepository.save(invoice);                              // ✅ Save AFTER publish
```

**Problem:** The domain event is published before the database transaction commits. If `save()` fails or the transaction rolls back, the event has already been sent to downstream consumers, creating a permanent inconsistency.

---

### ✅ Smallest Safe Fix: Outbox Pattern

**Add an outbox table and store events within the same transaction:**

#### 1. Add Outbox Entity (NEW)
```java
// src/main/java/com/example/invoice/DomainEventOutbox.java
package com.example.invoice;

import java.time.Instant;

public class DomainEventOutbox {
    private final String eventType;
    private final long aggregateId;
    private final Instant occurredAt;
    private final boolean published;

    public DomainEventOutbox(String eventType, long aggregateId) {
        this.eventType = eventType;
        this.aggregateId = aggregateId;
        this.occurredAt = Instant.now();
        this.published = false;
    }

    // getters...
}
```

#### 2. Add Outbox Repository (NEW)
```java
// src/main/java/com/example/invoice/DomainEventOutboxRepository.java
package com.example.invoice;

public interface DomainEventOutboxRepository {
    void save(DomainEventOutbox event);
}
```

#### 3. Update InvoiceService (MODIFY)
```java
// src/main/java/com/example/invoice/InvoiceService.java
public void approve(long invoiceId, String approver) {
    Invoice invoice = invoiceRepository.require(invoiceId);
    invoice.approve(approver, Instant.now());

    invoiceRepository.save(invoice);
    domainEventOutboxRepository.save(new DomainEventOutbox("invoice.approved", invoiceId));
    // ❌ Remove: domainEventPublisher.publish(...)
}
```

